    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on wolfram2002-ch12-48: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.40";
    dc:description "Existing images can test a narrow descriptive proxy, but they do not measure computational reducibility or the engineering motive claimed as the cause. The full explanation is therefore only partly resolvable.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    dc:type "resolution-route/empirical-data";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Construct matched image and dynamical datasets of artifacts and natural objects, quantify structural and predictive complexity, and relate artifact complexity to documented design requirements. A robust reversed difference challenges the descriptive part, but causal attribution requires controlling function, materials, and selection.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Function, scale, material, and selection confound natural-artifact comparisons.", "Image datasets do not contain engineering predictability requirements.", "Visual simplicity is metric-dependent.";
